  },
  "question": {
    "text": "If 1 mM solution of ethylamine produces $\\mathrm{pH}=9$, then the ionization constant $\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}}\\right)$ of ethylamine is $10^{-x}$. The value of $x$ is ______ (nearest integer).\n[The degree of ionization of ethylamine can be neglected with respect to unity.]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0012_2a0dbe213493.png\"><br>\n\n\n\nGiven, $\\mathrm{P}^{\\mathrm{H}}=9 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{P}^{\\mathrm{OH}}=5 \\Rightarrow[\\stackrel{\\ominus}{\\mathrm{OH}}]=10^{-5} \\mathrm{M}$\nNow, $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{\\left[\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{NH}_3^{+}\\right][\\stackrel{\\ominus}{\\mathrm{O}} \\mathrm{H}]}{\\left[\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{NH}_2\\right]}$\n$\\Rightarrow K_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{10^{-5} \\times 10^{-5}}{10^{-3}}=10^{-7}$"
  }
}